{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261001_111734_3579b0", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed the answer and linked paired-results and applicability artifacts.\n\nThis sharpens rather than overturns the cohort’s interpretation: the normal P5 reference does not reproduce the coordinated Nae1 antioxidant increase, but its near-null panel average conceals opposing Nqo1 and Hmox1 responses. Future summaries should retain individual-gene results and the four-subject, retrospective limitations.\n\nP7 Schwann-intrinsic attribution remains unidentified. Failed reference calibration cannot exclude real composition changes, and the pooled repair comparison remains a compartment warning with an unresolved handling alternative—not proof of a macrophage response.\n\nUpdated and synced LABBOOK for q_8ff898e6200c4b4a, attributing these findings to post_c65b70d5135e4002865bc16535c3377c. Existing negative and untestable results remain intact. No new investigation, duplicate follow-up or dispatch was initiated.", "tokens": {"input": 23482, "output": 2613, "total": 1494895, "cache_read": 1468800, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 102911, "timestamp": 1791227204781}
